  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p>At 322 feet, <strong>Bynum Mounds</strong> is a summit in Mississippi. The Bynum Mounds Trail covers 7.5 miles with about 164 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a gradual walk with modest climbing.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=33.91794,-88.94007\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">33.91794, -88.94007</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 195 miles southwest of Nashville, Tennessee. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>This trail is hikeable most of the year. Summer brings heat and humidity \u2014 carry extra water \u2014 while fall and spring offer the most comfortable conditions. Ice is possible on shaded stretches in mid-winter.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Easy rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 2.5 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Sand Mountain, Rocky Mountain and Little Mountain \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
